{
  /*
   * L0 storage — the one layer that keeps DOM, because knowing the platform is
   * its job.
   *
   * IndexedDB, BroadcastChannel and the quota estimate live here and nowhere
   * else; a config that took DOM away from this directory would fail
   * idb-driver.ts on the day it is written, and a gate that blocks the correct
   * implementation gets deleted along with the rules that were right.
   *
   * It still does not get `types`. vite/client and @types/node would let a
   * driver reach for `import.meta.env` or `fs`, and a storage adapter that can
   * read the filesystem is the Electron rewrite arriving early and by accident.
   * The extra strict flags from the base apply here too — this is the layer where
   * an unchecked index read is a row that silently is not there.
   *
   *
   * WHY THIS ONE IS `composite`, AND THE OTHER THREE ARE NOT
   *
   * `repo` reaches into this directory for four files — `driver.ts` (the port),
   * `memory-driver.ts` (the implementation of it that needs no platform),
   * `schema.ts` (the store catalogue) and `migrations.ts` — so storage is
   * reachable from a layer that compiles with no DOM at all. TypeScript
   * type-checks every file it reaches through an import, which means
   * `tsconfig.kg.json` would otherwise check `idb-driver.ts` under `"lib":
   * ["ES2023"]` and report `Cannot find name 'indexedDB'` against the one file
   * whose job is to name it. `exclude` is no help — it trims the initial file
   * set, not the import graph.
   *
   * (An earlier version of this note said `repo/boot.ts` imports
   * `createIdbDriver`. It does not: `boot()` takes `driver: Driver` and the web
   * app names the IndexedDB driver once, in `src/lib/store.tsx`. The reference
   * below is still load-bearing — just for the four files above, not for that
   * one.)
   *
   * `composite` is the mechanism that actually exists for this: the layer emits
   * a .d.ts, and its consumers type-check against THAT instead of against the
   * source. Which is the layer boundary restated as a build artifact — `repo`
   * sees `Driver`, and `Driver` is DOM-free by construction
   * (storage/driver.ts:24). The DOM stays on the other side of a declaration
   * file, exactly where the architecture says it stays.
   *
   * Declarations only, into node_modules/.tmp. Nothing is bundled from here —
   * vite still compiles the sources — so this emit is type-checking scaffolding
   * and belongs where the .tsbuildinfo already lives, not in dist/.
   */
  "extends": "./tsconfig.kg.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "tsBuildInfoFile": "./node_modules/.tmp/tsconfig.kg-storage.tsbuildinfo",
    "lib": ["ES2023", "DOM"],
    "types": [],

    "composite": true,
    "declaration": true,
    "emitDeclarationOnly": true,
    "noEmit": false,
    "rootDir": "./src/kg/storage",
    "outDir": "./node_modules/.tmp/kg-storage"
  },
  "include": ["src/kg/storage"]
}
